# DIT-OS kernel C++

Before editing matching files, read `.agents/skills/kernel-cpp/SKILL.md` and follow
it. Also apply `AGENTS.md` (definition of done, handoff, hard rules) and the
mandatory `.agents/skills/security-audit/SKILL.md` for every code change.
Content lives in the skill; this file only points to it.

Never forget:
- 32-bit only; namespaces are top level (core, mm, sched, fs, syscall, dev, arch).
- Never dereference user pointers: use mm::copy_from_user / copy_to_user.
- No exceptions, RTTI, new/delete, STL, floating point or SSE.
- Run scripts/qemu-test.sh and scripts/cppcheck.sh before calling it done.
